of Discrete Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050327 #edb/ref 1033 1388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050327 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4036942d-b5d5-592a-a620-1e02dcc440fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186158799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186158800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186158801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186158802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186158803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186158801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158798 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fdd49fee-8241-5a92-8763-eb72406aa943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158799 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{14}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158799 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158799 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "df20dc58-5b67-5b4a-a4b8-eca19f0be704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158800 #edb/ref 1080 "35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158800 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158800 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1253e8d1-5192-596f-970c-1553a00ebc59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158801 #edb/ref 1080 "70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158801 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158801 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2610e250-1e87-5e70-911e-ced87d38d5a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158802 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158802 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158802 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "322e03be-95c4-5fdf-9538-cfd90f4a2b3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158803 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7d810ec3-fb2e-5820-ae2e-d55f7775e2d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161856 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9111" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161856 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\textrm{Var}[4k^2-1]$ where $k$ is a constant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161856 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01fc4e2e-d93f-50b3-859e-19732d4f10c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161856 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[a] = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $k$ is a constant, $4k^2-1$ is also a constant, and we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[4k^2-1] = 0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161857 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161857 #edb/ref 1071 "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\textrm E[X] = 2.3,$ calculate $\\textrm{Var}[-10X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3f88c0e-9426-50d2-baf0-95909e222d4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161857 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX] = a^2\\cdot\\textrm{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-10X] & =(-10)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E[X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\textrm E [X] =2.3.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\textrm E[X^2].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X^2$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =1(0.2)+4(0.3)+9(0.5) \\\\  & =5.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.9-{(2.3)}^{2} \\\\  & =0.61.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-10X] & =100\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =100\\cdot 0.61 \\\\  & =61.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161858 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9114" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161858 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 10,$ calculate $\\textrm{Var}[1-2X].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161858 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c20c7b15-e967-52a9-846d-4915f6661158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161858 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+b] = a^2\\cdot\\textrm{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-2$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[1-2X] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186369036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186369043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186369050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186369057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186420136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186420139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing the Variance of a Constant" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162056 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "405984cd-1e1b-54c6-bc75-268e127b9812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162057 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162057 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1759218