nd $b=11.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[11-4X] & ={(-4)}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[11-4X] & =16\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186380802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186380798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380797 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "afffd28a-e3e8-51ad-b038-7186de3a8484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380798 #edb/ref 1080 "20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380798 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186380798 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ede9322-0ceb-5ef2-973b-006b6d2a855a" #edb/r